XR window: each eye's scene scissored to the window as that eye sees it (mode ventana)

In the window's frames (the mask's fade[3] 2) the scene's passes in each eye (the EFB passes with the
scene viewport) get a scissor to the bounds of the window's rectangle and of what may come out of it
(the rectangle narrowing toward the camera's eye, up to the pop-out), projected into that eye with a
margin of 5% of the picture a side, intersected with the game's own scissor: the pixels the mask
hides are no longer shaded. No scissor when a corner is at or behind the eye.
A viewport that takes no window scissor (a partial one) after one that did gets the game's own
scissor back.

